# Smart answer

Suggest a next check, not a diagnosis. A smart answer asks questions and uses the responses to route someone to a relevant outcome. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

Use [question pages](../../patterns/question-pages.html#compose-the-task-without-replacing-its-owner) for input, back navigation and retained answers. The examples do not configure native triggers, conditions or actions, and must not be described as an implemented automation or diagnostic editor.

## When to use it

Use a bounded decision aid to help people find existing guidance. Ask one meaningful question at a time, include "I do not know" where it fits and keep a route back to change an answer. For a simple choice between a few routes, see [Simple smart answer](smart-answer/simple-smart-answer.html). For version-controlled rules, see [GitHub smart answer](smart-answer/github-smart-answer.html).

## Structure and behaviour

Define every branch, outcome and prerequisite before you build the interaction. Keep earlier responses when someone goes back. Do not hide contradictory evidence, and do not give a confident recommendation from an unavailable reading ([WG-043](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-043)). Use a simple checklist when a decision tree adds no value.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme provides no diagnostic engine and does not infer appliance faults. The example choices go to explanatory text, not service calls. Safety decisions and device capability claims need verified domain guidance. A visual pattern cannot generate them.

